Approach 2 — Using Stack, But Searching From Left to Right

We can process prices from left to right and maintain indices whose discount has not yet been found.

For every current price:

while stack.top >= current price:
    stack.top gets current price as discount

Code
class Solution {
    public int[] finalPrices(int[] prices) {

        int n = prices.length;
        int[] ans = Arrays.copyOf(prices, n);

        Stack<Integer> st = new Stack<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            while (!st.isEmpty() && prices[st.peek()] >= prices[i]) {

                int index = st.pop();

                ans[index] = prices[index] - prices[i];
            }

            st.push(i);
        }

        return ans;
    }
}

